Metric:
- id: data.freshness
- name: 
- description: Data freshness measures the recency of data within tables relative to predefined refresh intervals, indicating how current the data is for analytical and operational purposes. This metric encompasses all data sources within the enterprise data platform, including both batch and real-time data ingestion processes. It typically signals the effectiveness of ETL/ELT pipelines and orchestration mechanisms in maintaining timely data updates. Common exclusions may include static reference data or historical datasets that do not require frequent updates. By monitoring data freshness, organizations can ensure that decision-making is based on the most relevant and timely information available.

