- description: This metric measures the extent to which data lineage tracking is implemented across various datasets within an enterprise data platform. It assesses the visibility of data transformations, movements, and dependencies from source to destination, ensuring that all data flows are documented and traceable. The scope includes both structured and unstructured data, as well as data processed through ETL/ELT pipelines and other data integration methods. Typical signals of completeness include the presence of metadata that captures the origin, transformations, and usage of data. Common exclusions may involve datasets that are not actively monitored or those that lack sufficient documentation, leading to potential gaps in lineage visibility.

