Metric:
- id: metadata.coverage
- name: 
- description: Metadata coverage measures the extent to which metadata fields are populated across various tables within a data platform. This metric evaluates the completeness and richness of metadata, which is crucial for data discovery, governance, and lineage tracking. It encompasses all relevant metadata attributes, such as data types, descriptions, and relationships, while excluding any non-standard or custom fields that may not be universally applicable. High metadata coverage indicates a well-documented data environment, facilitating better data management and compliance. Conversely, low coverage may signal gaps in documentation that could hinder data usability and trust.

