- description: The sensitive.tagging metric measures the extent to which sensitive data fields within an enterprise data platform are appropriately tagged for compliance with regulatory requirements. This includes identifying personal identifiable information (PII), financial data, and other sensitive categories that necessitate special handling. The scope encompasses all data storage and processing environments, including databases, data lakes, and ETL/ELT pipelines. Typical signals of compliance include the presence of metadata tags that indicate sensitivity levels and associated governance policies. Common exclusions may involve non-sensitive data fields or data that is not subject to regulatory scrutiny. This metric is crucial for ensuring data privacy, security, and adherence to legal obligations.

