- description: This metric evaluates the presence and reliability of backup and recovery mechanisms within an enterprise data platform. It measures the effectiveness of data protection strategies, including the frequency of backups, the integrity of backup data, and the success rate of recovery operations. The scope includes both on-premises and cloud-based storage solutions, as well as the orchestration processes that manage these backups. Typical signals include successful backup completion logs and recovery test results, while common exclusions may involve data that is not backed up due to policy constraints or operational oversight. This metric is crucial for ensuring data availability and compliance with governance standards.

