- description: The pipeline success rate measures the proportion of successful executions of data pipelines relative to the total number of executions within a defined time frame. This metric encompasses all types of pipeline runs, including those that perform Extract, Transform, Load (ETL) or Extract, Load, Transform (ELT) operations. It provides insights into the reliability and effectiveness of data workflows, helping to identify potential issues in data processing or orchestration. Common exclusions from this metric may include aborted runs or those that were intentionally skipped due to upstream dependencies. By monitoring this rate, organizations can assess the health of their data integration processes and make informed decisions regarding optimization and resource allocation.

