Metric:
- id: pipeline.latency_throughput
- name: 
- description: This metric measures the performance of data pipelines by evaluating both processing latency and throughput. Latency refers to the time taken for data to travel through the pipeline from ingestion to output, while throughput indicates the volume of data processed in a given time frame. The scope includes all stages of the pipeline, from data extraction to transformation and loading, capturing the efficiency of each component. Typical signals include variations in processing times and data volumes, which can indicate bottlenecks or inefficiencies. Common exclusions may involve external factors such as network delays or upstream data source performance that do not directly reflect the pipeline's internal processing capabilities.

