- description: Resource utilization measures the efficiency of compute, memory, and storage resources across clusters in relation to the financial expenditure incurred for these resources. It provides insights into how effectively the allocated resources are being used to support data processing and analytics workloads. This metric encompasses all active clusters within the enterprise data platform, capturing both on-demand and reserved resources. Typical signals include high utilization rates indicating efficient resource use, or low rates suggesting potential over-provisioning or underutilization. Common exclusions may involve idle resources or temporary spikes in usage that do not reflect ongoing operational patterns.

