Metric:
- id: query.performance
- name: 
- description: Query performance measures the efficiency of data retrieval operations by analyzing runtimes and failure rates across various workloads. This metric encompasses all executed queries within the data platform, providing insights into how quickly and reliably data can be accessed and processed. It includes both successful query executions and those that fail, allowing for a comprehensive view of performance issues. Typical signals may include prolonged runtimes or increased failure rates, which can indicate underlying problems in the data architecture or resource allocation. Common exclusions from this metric may involve queries that are not executed due to user errors or those that are intentionally designed to run for extended periods as part of testing or batch processing.

